{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `stoi`, `B`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that the parameter prior sampling statements for `beta`, `gamma`, `xi`, and `delta` occur before any model-block computation that uses the ODE solution `y`, which depends on those parameters. The protected observations `stoi` and `B` remain top-level data variables and are each observed exactly once with built-in sampling statements. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"// Simple SIR model inspired by the presentation in
// http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3380087/pdf/nihms372789.pdf

functions {
  vector simple_SIR(real t, vector y, real beta,
                    // water contact rate
                    real kappa, // C_{50}
                    real gamma, // recovery rate
                    real xi, // bacteria production rate
                    real delta) {
    // bacteria removal rate
    vector[4] dydt;

    dydt[1] = -beta * y[4] / (y[4] + kappa) * y[1];
    dydt[2] = beta * y[4] / (y[4] + kappa) * y[1] - gamma * y[2];
    dydt[3] = gamma * y[2];
    dydt[4] = xi * y[2] - delta * y[4];

    return dydt;
  }
}
data {
  int<lower=0> N_t;
  array[N_t] real t;
  vector[4] y0;
  array[N_t] int stoi;
  array[N_t] real B;
}
transformed data {
  real t0 = 0;
  real<lower=0> kappa = 1000000;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> beta;
  real<lower=0> gamma;
  real<lower=0> xi;
  real<lower=0> delta;
}
transformed parameters {
  array[N_t] vector<lower=0>[4] y = ode_rk45_tol(simple_SIR, y0, t0, t, 1e-6,
                                                 1e-6, 1000, beta, kappa,
                                                 gamma, xi, delta);
}
model {
  vector[N_t] y_diff;

  beta ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  gamma ~ cauchy(0, 1);
  xi ~ cauchy(0, 25);
  delta ~ cauchy(0, 1);

  y_diff[1] = y0[1] - y[1, 1];
  for (n in 2 : N_t) {
    y_diff[n] = y[n - 1, 1] - y[n, 1];
  }

  stoi ~ poisson(y_diff);
  B ~ lognormal(log(y[ : , 4]), 0.15);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"B":[3.457432205284768,3.5533217724090913,0.30000000000000004,0.4],"N_t":4,"stoi":[2,6,1,1],"t":[1.0,2.0,3.0,4.0],"y0":[4.945932822088683,5.306325580104025,4.141993571911474,6.902247546327437]}","protected_variables":["stoi","B"]}
